DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggeettppeeeerrnnaammee() system call returns the name of the peer connected to
     socket _s.  The _n_a_m_e_l_e_n argument should be initialized to indicate the
     amount of space pointed to by _n_a_m_e.  On return it contains the actual
     size of the name returned (in bytes).  The name is truncated if the buf‐
     fer provided is too small.

